#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# differential_reduce

#% text
# `differential_reduce(p, ps, u, x)` gives the full remainder of the differential polynomial `p` with respect to the differential polynomials `ps` in the functions `u` of `x`: proper derivatives of the leaders of `ps` are eliminated with the derivatives of `ps` (multiplying by separants), then the degrees in the leaders are lowered by pseudo-division (multiplying by initials).

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The remainder is defined up to a factor of the base field. For a regular differential chain `ps` it is 0 exactly when `p` lies in the differential ideal of `ps` saturated by their initials and separants (Ritt; Kolchin, Differential Algebra and Algebraic Groups, I.9).

#% item
# The ranking is `ranking: orderly` (the default) or `ranking: elimination`, as for `differential_leader`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
differential_reduce(y''(x), [y'(x)^2 - 4*y(x)], y, x)
#% output
#= y'(x)

#% cell
differential_reduce(y'(x)^3, [y'(x)^2 - 4*y(x)], y, x)
#% output
#= y(x)*y'(x)

#% text
# A member of the differential ideal reduces to 0:

#% cell
differential_reduce(d(y'(x)^2 - 4*y(x), x, x), [y'(x)^2 - 4*y(x)], y, x)
#% output
#= 0

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `delta_polynomial`, `rosenfeld_groebner`, `differential_leader`
